  "id": "Compound::DB00835 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Brompheniramine, a nasal decongestant, is shown to bind to Cyp2c19 and Cyp2d6, both of which are involved in the oxidation of arachidonic acid. These enzymes are part of the arachidonic acid monooxygenase and epoxygenase pathways, which are critical for the production of pro-inflammatory mediators. The shared involvement of Cyp2c19 and Cyp2d6 in these pathways suggests a potential overlap in their enzymatic functions, which may explain why Brompheniramine could influence the metabolic processing of arachidonic acid. The evidence indicates that Cyp2e1, a key enzyme in the arachidonic acid metabolism, is a downstream participant in these pathways, suggesting a possible dependency on the activity of Cyp2c19 and Cyp2d6. This integrated pathway highlights the role of these enzymes in the metabolic cascade leading to the production of inflammatory mediators, and the relationship between Brompheniramine and Cyp2e1 may be mediated through these intermediate steps.",
